UPDATE companies SET description='Solar FX is headquartered in Boone, Iowa. The company was founded in 2008 by Gary Lass as a small family-owned business that began by installing solar-powered attic fans and residential solar arrays. In July 2023, Lass sold the business to his children, Jeremy (known as Oly) and Charise Lass; Charise later acquired full ownership while Jeremy remains as a field supervisor and Gary continues as an advisor.

Today Solar FX operates as a turnkey solar contractor, providing design, engineering, sales, and installation of photovoltaic (PV) arrays for agricultural, commercial, and utility-scale projects. All installations are carried out by in-house crews using company-owned equipment, and the firm manages the full permitting process, utility interconnection applications, and coordination with local jurisdictions.

The customer base spans hog barn operators, livestock farms, commercial facilities, and utility developers throughout the Midwest. Testimonials cite successful projects on agricultural sites such as a hog barn and a private acreage, as well as commercial installations.

Solar FX says its competitive pricing stems from buying panels directly from the importer of record, supplying only Tier One modules listed on the Bloomberg tier list, and remaining brand-agnostic to select the optimal panels, inverters, and racking for each custom-designed system.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Customized design and installation services", "Solar energy design", "Engineering", "Sales", "Photovoltaic (PV) array installation", "Permitting management", "Utility interconnection applications", "Municipal coordination", "Site assessment"], "industries": ["Agricultural", "Commercial", "Industrial", "Utility-scale"], "materials": ["Photovoltaic modules (Tier One)", "Inverters", "Racking systems"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Direct purchasing from importer of record for competitive pricing", "Tier One solar panels (Bloomberg list)", "Custom-designed arrays for each site", "Brand-agnostic equipment selection", "In-house installation crews and equipment", "Full permitting and interconnection management"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Boone, Iowa -> db, /about-us", "Founded 2008 by Gary Lass -> /about-us", "Family-owned and operated -> /about-us, / (testimonial)", "Ownership transition to Jeremy and Charise Lass in 2023 -> /about-us", "Turnkey solar design, engineering, sales, installation -> /about-us", "In-house staff and equipment for installations -> /about-us", "Permitting, interconnection, municipal coordination handled -> /about-us", "Industries: agricultural, commercial, utility-scale -> /about-us", "Customer examples: hog barn, livestock operation, acreage -> / (testimonials)", "Direct purchasing from importer of record -> /about-us", "Tier One panels (Bloomberg list) -> /about-us", "Brand-agnostic equipment selection -> /about-us", "Custom-designed arrays per site -> /about-us", "Team members: Charise Bailey, Gary Lass, Jeremy Lass, Preston Stamp, Teresa Mueller -> /about-us", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "SOLAR FX became a turnkey solar company specializing in solar energy design, engineering, sales, and installation.", "founded_year": "2008", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/solarfxinc/"], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='solar-fx' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='SON Metal Fab operates from Ashland, Virginia, just north of Richmond. The business traces its roots to Butch Harrison, who founded the company as Specialty''s Our Name with the strong support of his family; it later adopted the SON Metal Fab name. A founding year is not publicly disclosed.

The shop provides custom sheet metal fabrication, welding, machining, and manufacturing services. Its capabilities include laser cutting, CNC punching, CNC bending, rolling, deburring, and powder coating, along with precision parts production. Equipment on the floor features a ¼″–10′ AccurShear with CNC controls, a Hurco CNC lathe with bar feeder, and a Hurco machining center. The company does not publish facility size, headcount, or annual volume figures.

SON Metal Fab serves a broad range of clients in the Richmond, Virginia area. The website does not list specific industry sectors or named customers, focusing instead on local and regional project work of varying duration.

