UPDATE companies SET description='STI Electronics, Inc. was founded in 1982 by Jim D. Raby, P.E., in San Dimas, California. The family-run business relocated to Madison, Alabama, in 1993 and has since grown to over fifty professionals. Raby brought more than 55 years of industry experience, including a pivotal role in developing NASA and Department of Defense soldering schools.

The company provides contract electronic manufacturing, engineering and design services, rapid prototyping, new product introduction (NPI) builds, PCB assembly, rework and repair, advanced testing, and conformal coating.

STI serves safety-critical, mission-critical, and military-grade applications across aerospace, defense, medical, industrial, and energy markets. Customers include organizations requiring high-reliability cable and wire harness assemblies, PCB assemblies, and specialized engineering support for low-to-medium volume, high-complexity programs.

