UPDATE companies SET description='Sana Packaging operates from Denver, Colorado, specializing in full-service cannabis packaging. The company does not publicly disclose its founding year, ownership structure, or the names of its founders.

The company produces a range of cannabis packaging including jars, bottles, and flexible pouches made from post-consumer recycled (PCR) plastic and reclaimed ocean-bound plastic. Its capabilities encompass extrusion and molding, label printing and application, direct printing, in-mold labeling, custom flexible pouches, and custom paperboard displays. Sana Packaging reports having reclaimed over 768,000 pounds of ocean-bound plastic and maintains on-hand inventory with low minimum order quantities for stock items.

The company also partners with HempPress and Tree Hugger Containers to offer additional product lines, all warehoused and shipped from domestic locations.

The company differentiates itself through a ''no silly business, no hidden fees, and no BS'' policy, emphasizing transparent pricing, quick turnaround times, and sustainability. It highlights responsible material sourcing, waste-reducing design, and end-of-life recoverability as core to its approach, alongside next-business-day shipping for blank in-stock products.', certifications=ARRAY['Child-resistant certified','FDA-compliant materials']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Full-service cannabis packaging", "Custom cannabis packaging", "Custom packaging services", "Extrusion and molding", "Label printing", "Label application", "Direct printing", "In-mold labeling", "Custom flexible pouches", "Custom paperboard displays", "Artwork and dieline support", "Packaging coordination"], "industries": ["Cannabis", "Cannabis packaging"], "materials": ["Post-consumer recycled (PCR) plastic", "Ocean-bound plastic", "Food-grade plastic", "FDA-compliant materials"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Next business day for blank in-stock products; custom lead times vary after proof approval", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["No hidden fees, transparent pricing", "Next-business-day shipping on blank in-stock products", "Reclaimed over 768,000 lbs of ocean-bound plastic", "Child-resistant, FDA-compliant materials", "End-to-end customization including label printing, direct printing, and in-mold labeling"], "facts_used": ["Location: Denver, Colorado (db)", "Reclaimed 768,000+ lbs ocean-bound plastic (homepage)", "Offers extrusion & molding (homepage)", "Provides label printing, direct printing, in-mold labeling (homepage)", "Child-resistant certified, FDA-compliant materials (homepage)", "Next business day shipping for blank in-stock (homepage)", "Partners with HempPress and Tree Hugger Containers (homepage)", "Low MOQs, transparent pricing (homepage)"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Pellets Are Molded Into New Products: The pellets are molded into new products, like packaging.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "Varies by product; blank in-stock by the case", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/sana-packaging/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sana-packaging' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Sandbox VT is based in the south end of Burlington, Vermont, where it runs a repair and circular services operation from a storefront The venture began as a creators space promoting sustainable action through creativity and community, though the exact founding year and ownership structure are not specified in public materials.

The business provides a range of textile repair and restoration services for both individuals and commercial clients. For consumers, offerings include clothing repair, technical outerwear and gear repair, backpack repair, zipper replacement, alterations, and a mail‑in repair option. For brands, retailers, and designers, Sandbox VT runs warranty and repair programs, provides overflow repair capacity, performs technical sewing, product restoration, waterproofing, returns refurbishment, and executes small‑batch production runs using upcycled brand sample fabric. The company also curates a monthly marketplace of gently pre‑loved apparel.

Clients span individual consumers seeking to extend the life of personal garments, as well as outdoor brands, retailers, and designers who prioritize durability and circularity. The company explicitly mentions working with outdoor brands and retailers that believe in quality and doing better, and it serves designers needing small‑batch production from sample materials.

