UPDATE companies SET description='Sander''s Sew-N-Vac + The Fabric Bin operates from a downtown storefront in Aberdeen, South Dakota. The business traces its roots to 1945 when Al Sander opened Sander''s Sew-N-Vac to sell Electrolux vacuums. In 1976 his son Greg Sander purchased the shop and, in the late 1990s, expanded into fabric retail under the name The Fabric Bin. The company remains a family-owned proprietorship, now managed by Greg with support from longtime employees Shirelle Stadel and Alesha Stadel.

The store carries hundreds of bolts of fabric alongside notions, pre-cut kits, and sewing supplies, and also runs an e‑commerce site with live‑streamed shopping events. In‑store services include weekly live shows, sewing classes, and personalized project assistance. The physical location is open Tuesday through Saturday with limited hours, and the business offers 0% interest financing through a third‑party partner.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Fabric retail", "Notions retail", "Sewing kit assembly", "Sewing classes", "Live streaming sales events", "Project consulting"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned since 1945", "Hundreds of fabric bolts in stock", "Weekly live shopping shows", "Sewing classes and project assistance", "0% interest financing available"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1945 by Al Sander -> /", "Greg Sander purchased store in 1976 -> /", "Expanded to fabric retail late 1990s/early 2000s -> /", "Store holds hundreds of bolts of fabric -> /", "Location: 111 South Main St, Aberdeen SD 57401 -> /", "Family-owned proprietorship -> /", "Employees: Greg Sander, Shirelle Stadel (10 years), Alesha Stadel (4 years) -> /", "Offers fabrics, notions, kits, classes, live shows -> /", "0% interest financing via Synchrony -> /", "Store hours Tuesday-Saturday -> /"], "company_type": "Retailer", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Greg Sander purchased the downtown main-street store from his dad in 1976. Al Sander opened Sander''s Sew-N-Vac in 1945 selling Electrolux vacuums. Greg then expanded the business by selling Fabric; in the late 1990s/early 2000''s Greg opened the The Fabric Bin. Today the store holds over hundreds of bolts of fabric!", "founded_year": "1945", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=no