UPDATE companies SET description='Sapphire Systems Inc. was incorporated in 2007 by Charles Allmon and John Outwater in a garage laboratory to commercialize crystal-growth innovations. The company soon moved to a larger facility in Bedford, Massachusetts, along the Route 128 corridor northwest of Boston, to develop larger systems and begin commercial production.

The company grows optical-quality sapphire plates using the Edge-defined, Film-fed Growth (EFG) method, which it considers ideal for large-area plates. Current production yields plates 15‑5/8 inches wide, with standard plates of 30 by 15‑5/8 inches by 3/8 inch thick planned for pilot production; larger plates are available on request. Sapphire Systems has also produced and sold optical sapphire fiber and sapphire ribbon for superconductor substrates.

Its customers span military and commercial markets. For defense, the firm supplies sensor windows, transparent armor, and bullet‑proof windows used on range finders, infrared cameras, and personnel protection systems. In semiconductor manufacturing, its sapphire components serve as windows, wafer carriers, and other hardware that withstand corrosive chip‑fabrication environments.

Sapphire Systems differentiates itself through its patented EFG growth technology and the scale of its plates, which it describes as among the largest commercially available. The company holds three U.S. patents, an R&D 100 Award, and an SBIR Award for its superconducting wire epitaxial growth process.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Edge-defined Film-fed Growth (EFG)", "Large-area sapphire plate production", "Sapphire fiber production", "Sapphire ribbon production", "Sensor window manufacturing", "Transparent armor manufacturing", "Semiconductor wafer carrier manufacturing"], "industries": ["Military", "Semiconductor Manufacturing", "Commercial"], "materials": ["Sapphire (Al2O3)", "Aluminum oxide", "Corundum", "Sapphire fiber", "Sapphire ribbon"], "equipment": ["Integrated Crucible and Die System", "Targeted Heat Control System", "Thermal Chimney", "Feed System", "Window Holder"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Growing some of the largest commercially-available sapphire plates in the world", "Edge-defined, Film-fed Growth (EFG) method for large-area plates", "Three U.S. patents awarded plus R&D 100 Award and SBIR Award", "Optical-quality sapphire plates up to 30 x 15-5/8 inches", "Produced optical sapphire fiber and ribbon for superconductor substrates"], "facts_used": ["Incorporated in 2007 by Charles Allmon and John Outwater -> /", "Moved to Bedford, MA to develop larger systems and start commercial production -> /", "Grows optical-quality sapphire plates using EFG method -> /", "Current plates 15-5/8 inches wide; standard plates 30 x 15-5/8 x 3/8 inches planned -> /", "Produced and sold optical sapphire fiber and ribbon for superconductor substrates -> /", "Serves military customers for sensor windows, transparent armor, bullet-proof windows -> /", "Serves semiconductor manufacturing for windows, wafer carriers, hardware -> /", "Awarded three US patents, R&D 100 Award, SBIR Award -> /", "Patents: Apparatus and Methods of Growing Void-Free Crystalline Ceramic Products, Targeted Heat Control System, Integrated Crucible and Die System, Window Holder, Thermal Chimney, Feed System -> /", "Headquarters: Bedford, Massachusetts -> db", "Founded year 2007 -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Sapphire Systems has developed technology to grow some of the largest sapphire plates in the world.", "founded_year": "2007", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sapphire-systems-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Sasquatch Water Company, LLC operates from Redmond, Oregon, delivering purified alkaline drinking water and bagged ice to customers throughout Central Oregon. The company also designs and builds the Diamond Skid, an industrial-grade reverse osmosis system sold in domestic and international markets.

The core service is a 12-step reverse osmosis filtration process that employs more than 50 individual filters to produce alkaline water with a pH of 8.8. The process includes pre-filtration down to 20 microns, carbon filtration, a 5-micron pre-filter, a high-pressure stainless steel RO pump, a .0002-micron membrane, UV sterilization, and optional ozone treatment. Water is stored in FDA-approved tanks and repressurized for consistent delivery. In addition to water, the company produces two styles of bagged ice: Cristal Clear half-dome and nugget ice. On the equipment side, the Diamond Skid line features a powder-coated steel frame, prewired electrical panel, stainless steel booster pump, and components that carry NSF, FDA, UL, or ETL approvals. Models share a common footprint of 90″L × 30″W × 74″H and can be customized with feed pumps, TDS meters, water softeners, and chemical injection.

Residential and commercial customers in Central Oregon subscribe to 24/7 water delivery, while the Diamond Skid systems serve domestic and international buyers needing turnkey water purification for bottling, vending, or industrial processes.

Sasquatch Water emphasizes purity and affordability, citing independent lab certification of its water and a filtration train designed to remove 99.9% of impurities from source, plumbing, and municipal lines. The Diamond Skid was developed to answer the call for pure, quality, consumable drinking water in varied feed-water conditions, with recovery rates up to 60% and salt rejection of 90–98%.', certifications=ARRAY['NSF/FDA/UL/ETL approved components','Independent lab certified purity']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["12-step reverse osmosis filtration", "Alkaline water production (pH 8.8)", "Bagged ice manufacturing (Cristal Clear half-dome, Nugget ice)", "Industrial reverse osmosis system manufacturing (Diamond Skid)", "Water delivery service (24/7)", "Pre-filtration (20 micron AG, 5 micron)", "Carbon filtration (chlorine, chloramine, solvents, lead removal)", "High-pressure RO pump (160 psi)", "Reverse osmosis membrane (.0002 micron)", "UV sterilization (99.9% bacteria elimination)", "Ozone treatment (optional)", "Post carbon filtration (coconut shell carbon block)", "Repressure system (12 GPM)", "Storage in FDA-approved tanks", "Customizable feed water treatment (feed pump, water softener, chemical injection)", "TDS monitoring", "Hour metering"], "industries": ["Residential and commercial water delivery", "Industrial water purification equipment"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Diamond Skid reverse osmosis system", "AG Pre-Filtration (20 micron)", "Carbon Filtration", "5 Micron Pre-Filter", "R.O. Pump (stainless steel, 160 psi)", "Reverse Osmosis Membrane (.0002 micron)", "FDA-approved storage tanks", "Repressure System (12 GPM)", "Pressure Tank (32-gallon)", "Post Carbon Filtration (coconut shell carbon block)", "Ultraviolet Sterilizer", "Ozone generator (optional)", "Feed pump", "TDS meter", "Hour meter", "Water softener"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["12-step reverse osmosis filtration with 50+ individual filters", "24/7 water delivery service across Central Oregon", "Independent lab certified water purity", "Two proprietary bagged ice formats (Cristal Clear half-dome, Nugget ice)", "Diamond Skid industrial RO systems with NSF/FDA/UL/ETL approved components"], "facts_used": ["Location: Redmond, OR -> db", "12-step RO filtration with 50+ filters -> /", "Alkaline water pH 8.8 -> /", "Bagged ice: Cristal Clear half-dome and Nugget ice -> /", "Diamond Skid industrial RO system -> /services", "Diamond Skid components NSF/FDA/UL/ETL approved -> /services", "24/7 water delivery -> /", "Independent lab certified purity -> /", "Diamond Skid specifications (recovery up to 60%, salt rejection 90-98%) -> /services", "Headquarters address 1737 SW Odem Medo Redmond OR 97756 -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We make 2 kinds of Ice. Cristal Clear, half round ice, and Nugget Ice. The Diamond Skid is an industrial grade reverse osmosis water purification system.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sasquatch-water-company-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Saturn PCB Design, Inc. is headquartered in DeBary, Florida. The company is led by President Kenneth J. Wood. A founding year is not publicly disclosed.

The company provides printed circuit board design, manufacturing, and assembly services, along with comprehensive electronic engineering. Its design capabilities span RF circuits, digital designs including DSP and FPGA, and low-level analog circuits. Manufacturing covers single-, double-, and multi-layer boards, while assembly delivers finished boards with components soldered. The firm also offers Design for Manufacture, Test, and Assembly (DFX) analysis, signal integrity management, and impedance control, using tools such as Altium Designer, Cadence Allegro, and Mentor HyperLynx.

Saturn PCB serves customers worldwide across military, space, medical, industrial, and commercial sectors. The company emphasizes secure PCB solutions that meet government regulations for national security, cybersecurity, and supply chain transparency.

