UPDATE companies SET description='SauceWorks is a small-batch gourmet sauce producer and full-scale co-packing facility based in Tacoma, Washington. The company operates an FDA-registered facility where it manufactures its own line of hot sauces, seasonings, and dry rubs while also providing contract manufacturing services for other brands.

The facility houses professional-grade stainless steel equipment designed to ensure consistent viscosity, precise pH balance, and rigorous sanitation across every batch. SauceWorks handles both small and large production runs, offering end-to-end co-packing that includes recipe scaling, bottling, labeling, and regulatory compliance. Its product portfolio spans hot sauces such as a chipotle blend and the Carolina Reaper–based Fear The Reaper, as well as dry rubs and seasonings sold directly to consumers.

The company serves two primary customer groups: retail buyers who purchase SauceWorks-branded products through its online store, and food brands seeking a co-packing partner to bring their own recipes to market.

SauceWorks differentiates itself by emphasizing industrial-grade standards in a facility that exceeds typical home-kitchen operations, sourcing real peppers without fillers or artificial thickeners, and promising same-day shipment on direct orders with free shipping over $50. The founders’ stated philosophy is that heat should elevate flavor rather than overwhelm it.', certifications=ARRAY['FDA Registered']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Co-packing", "Recipe scaling", "Bottling", "Labeling", "Regulatory compliance support", "Sauce production", "Seasoning production", "Private labeling", "Small batch production", "Large batch production"], "industries": ["Food and beverage manufacturing", "Specialty foods", "Hot sauce", "Seasonings", "Private label food products"], "materials": ["Fresh-smoked Chipotle peppers", "Carolina Reaper peppers", "Roasted tomatoes", "Caramelized onions", "Fresh garlic", "Spices"], "equipment": [], "volume": "Small or large production runs", "lead_time": "Same-day shipping on direct orders", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["FDA-registered facility with professional-grade stainless steel machinery", "Consistent viscosity, precise pH balance, and rigorous sanitation in every batch", "Real peppers, no fillers or artificial thickeners; natural ingredients only", "Same-day shipping on direct orders; free shipping on orders over $50", "End-to-end co-packing including recipe scaling, bottling, labeling, and compliance"], "facts_used": ["Located in Tacoma, Washington -> db", "FDA registered -> db", "Produces gourmet hot sauces and seasonings -> homepage", "Offers co-packing services including recipe scaling, bottling, labeling, compliance -> homepage", "Same-day shipping on orders -> homepage", "Free shipping on orders over $50 -> homepage", "Uses natural ingredients: fresh-smoked Chipotles, Carolina Reapers, roasted tomatoes, caramelized onions, fresh garlic -> homepage", "Operates fully modern FDA-registered facility with professional-grade stainless steel machinery -> homepage", "Small or large production runs -> homepage"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Small Batch Gourmet Sauce Producer And Full Scale Co-Packing Facility", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sauceworks' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Sauder Furniture and Design Studio operates from a 20,000-square-foot showroom in Roanoke, Illinois, a small town in the central part of the state. The business traces its roots to 1907, when Grandpa Sauder opened the original store, and it has remained family-owned ever since. Today the company is led by fifth-generation owner Wade Sauder, who serves as president and customer relations associate, and fourth-generation co-owner Jeff Sauder, who oversees customer relations and flooring installation.

The store functions as a full-service furniture retailer and design studio. Its product assortment includes sofas, loveseats, chairs, recliners, sectionals, bedroom sets, mattresses, and dining-room pieces, along with a flooring selection covering carpet, hardwood, luxury vinyl plank, and tile. Beyond sales, the staff provides interior design consulting, measure-and-install services, and a professional installation team that handles everything from flooring to window treatments. Home decor, candles, and fashion accessories round out the offering.

The customer base is primarily residential, drawing from Roanoke and the surrounding Central Illinois region, with a broader reach across the Midwest. The company emphasizes its role as a community fixture, serving neighbors and friends through a team that includes in-house designers, delivery and installation crews, and customer relations specialists.

The Sauder family positions the business on a tradition of personal service that spans generations. Wade Sauder describes great customer service not just as a tradition but as a way of life, while Jeff Sauder highlights trust, relationships, and making every customer feel like part of the family. That heritage, combined with a full-service model under one roof, is presented as the core differentiator.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Retail furniture sales", "Flooring sales and installation", "Interior design consulting", "Delivery and set-up", "Measure and install services", "Home decor and accessories retail"], "industries": ["Residential furniture retail", "Flooring retail and installation", "Home decor retail", "Interior design services"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned and operated for five generations", "20,000 sq ft full-service furniture store and design studio", "In-house interior designers and professional installation team", "Measure-and-install services for flooring and window treatments", "Broad product range including furniture, flooring, home decor, and accessories"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1907 by Grandpa Sauder -> /about-us", "Family-owned business, now fifth generation (Wade Sauder) and fourth generation (Jeff Sauder) -> /about-us", "Located in Roanoke, Illinois, 20,000 sq ft full-service furniture store and design studio -> /about-us", "Offers furniture categories: sofas, loveseats, chairs, recliners, sectionals, bedroom, mattresses, dining -> /", "Offers flooring: carpet, hardwood, LVP, tile -> /", "Provides measure and install services, delivery and set-up, interior design consulting -> /about-us, /", "Team includes in-house designers, delivery, installation, customer relations specialists -> /about-us", "Serves residential customers in Illinois and Midwest, Central Illinois area -> /about-us", "Emphasizes family tradition of customer service, trust, relationships -> /about-us", "Social media handles: Instagram and Facebook @ShopSauderFurniture -> /"], "company_type": "Retailer", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "unique 20,000 square foot full-service furniture store and design studio", "founded_year": "1907", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sauder-furniture-and-design-studio' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Saunders Machine Works is based in Zanesville, Ohio, where it develops and produces workholding hardware for CNC machining.

Its catalog centers on SMW fixture plates, a modular vise line called Mod Vise that offers smooth, serrated, and soft jaws along with custom pallets and fixtures, and the PuckChuck zero-point clamping system available in automatic and mechanical receiver models. The company also offers traditional CNC vises, accessory kits, quick-change fixturing components, pallets, and fixture pins.

Saunders Machine Works highlights benefits such as decreased spindle downtime, higher parts-per-cycle throughput, and full use of the machine work envelope. The product design incorporates color-coded plugs for repeatable setups, diamond pins for rapid alignment, and a modular vise system that removes the need for vise tramming.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom pallet and fixture fabrication", "Quick-change fixturing", "Modular vise systems", "Zero-point clamping systems", "Fixture plate production"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Color-coded plugs for repeatable setups", "Diamond pins for fast alignment", "Modular vise system eliminates vise tramming", "Low-profile modular zero-point clamping (PuckChuck)", "Custom pallets and fixtures available"], "facts_used": ["Location: Zanesville, Ohio -> db", "Product: SMW fixture plates and workholding products -> db, /", "Product lines: Mod Vises, PuckChuck zero-point system, traditional CNC vises, accessory kits, quick-change fixturing, pallets, fixture pins -> /", "Mod Vise features: smooth jaws, serrated jaws, soft jaws, custom pallets & fixtures -> /", "PuckChuck system: low-profile modular zero-point clamping, automatic and mechanical receivers -> /", "Marketing claims: decrease spindle downtime, machine more parts per cycle, maximize machine work envelope, improve setup time, color-coded plugs, diamond pins, no vise tramming -> /", "Contact email:  -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Optimize your setup with SMW fixture plates and work holding products.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='saunders-machine-works' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Savant Manufacturing Inc. is based in Kinder, Louisiana. The company traces its roots to 1978 when founder Kevin Savant, then 14, built his first four-wheeler rack in his backyard using homemade tools and scrap metal. After years of part-time orders, the business was formalized in 1985 with a workshop on Highway 383 in Kinder, starting with one employee. The company remains a self-made, founder-owned operation.

SMI operates as a full-service metal fabrication and machine shop, offering laser cutting (including a 6 kW fiber laser), CNC bending (press brakes up to 12 feet wide), CNC milling and turning (Haas equipment), turret punching (two machines), plasma cutting, robotic welding, powder coating (automated line accommodating parts up to 60 inches wide), sanding, deburring, and PEM hardware insertion. The shop also provides engineering and design support using SolidWorks and AutoCAD, and maintains a FARO Arm CMM for inspection. They handle prototype through production volumes, with the capacity to produce thousands of parts under one roof.

The company originally specialized in ATV and UTV accessories—front and rear racks, drop racks, floor boards, gun racks, stick shifts, and similar items—custom-fitted to new models each year. Today, SMI serves a broader range of clients as a job shop, manufacturing, modifying, and repairing prototype and production parts for various industries across the southern United States, leveraging a network of partner shops for processes not performed in-house.

SMI emphasizes a quality system built on hiring for attitude, quality, cooperation, and growth, with quarterly employee reviews and multi-stage inspections (welders, buffers, painters, packers, shippers). The founder’s early experience shaped a culture of double-checking every weld and finish, and the automated powder-coat line ensures consistent, durable finishes. The company states its differentiator is a precise mix of quality, service, delivery, and price, staying on the cutting edge of manufacturing technology.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Laser cutting (6 kW fiber laser)", "CNC press brake bending (up to 12 ft wide)", "CNC milling", "CNC turning", "CNC turret punching (two machines)", "Plasma cutting", "Robotic welding", "Production welding (MIG/TIG)", "Powder coating (automated line, up to 60 in wide)", "Sanding and deburring", "PEM hardware insertion", "CMM inspection (FARO Arm)", "Engineering and design (SolidWorks, AutoCAD)", "Saw cutting", "Drilling and tapping", "Plate cutting and forming", "Pipe bending", "Custom tooling and fixture fabrication", "Prototyping", "Production machining"], "industries": ["ATV/UTV accessories"], "materials": ["Aluminum", "Stainless Steel", "Carbon Steel"], "equipment": ["FARO Arm CMM", "6 kW Fiber Laser", "Haas CNC machining centers", "Two CNC turret punches", "CNC press brakes (up to 12 ft capacity)", "Automated powder coating line (60 in wide)", "Robotic welding cells", "CNC plasma cutter with scribing feature", "Sanding/deburring equipment", "SolidWorks and AutoCAD design stations"], "volume": "Prototype to mass production (thousands of parts)", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Multi-stage inspection: welds checked by welder, buffer, painter, packer, and shipper", "Automated powder-coat line with chemical cleaning, rinsing, and baking", "In-house engineering and design using SolidWorks and AutoCAD", "Network of machine shops across the South for processes not done in-house"