UPDATE companies SET description='Sawdust & Splinters LLC operates from Sioux Falls, South Dakota, where it handcrafts custom dining tables, benches, chairs, and matching furniture. The workshop builds each piece to order, starting with the customer''s space rather than a stock size chart.

The company works exclusively with solid hardwoods such as walnut, oak, alder, beech, maple, and white oak, offering a range of natural, stained, painted, and custom-matched finishes. Its process moves from a design consultation through detailed specifications for size, base style, wood species, and seating options, after which the project enters a production queue for handcrafted assembly and finishing in Sioux Falls.

The business serves homeowners and families seeking heirloom-quality dining furniture tailored to their specific rooms and usage patterns. Clients provide inspiration photos, dimensions, and material preferences, and the shop translates those into one-of-a-kind tables, benches, and chairs.

Sawdust & Splinters emphasizes that its pieces are built for real family life, combining quality joinery with finishes selected for durability and everyday practicality. The company also offers a line of cleaning and maintenance products formulated for its furniture.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture design", "Solid wood joinery", "Custom finishing (stain, paint, custom match)", "Custom sizing and layout planning", "Chair and bench fabrication"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Walnut", "Oak", "Alder", "Beech", "Maple", "White Oak"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Every piece starts with the customer''s home, not a stock size chart", "Handcrafted in Sioux Falls using solid hardwoods and quality joinery", "Finishes chosen to fit real family life", "Custom design consultation covering size, base style, wood species, and seating", "Production queue system for approved designs"], "facts_used": ["Location: Sioux Falls, South Dakota -> db", "Handcrafts custom dining tables, benches, chairs, matching furniture -> /", "Uses solid hardwoods: walnut, oak, alder, beech, maple, white oak -> /", "Offers custom finishes: natural, stained, painted, custom-matched -> /", "Custom order process: share vision, dial details, join build queue -> /", "Sells cleaning and maintenance products -> db", "Serves homeowners and families seeking heirloom-quality dining furniture -> /", "Emphasizes quality joinery and finishes for durability and everyday practicality -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our work is handcrafted in Sioux Falls using solid hardwoods, quality joinery, and finishes chosen to fit real family life.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sawdust-splinters-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Sawyer Made operates from East Calais, Vermont. The company was formally launched in 2012 by George Sawyer, building on a chairmaking lineage that began in 1982 when his father, Dave Sawyer, an MIT-trained mechanical engineer, built his first Windsor chair. Dave spent three decades refining Windsor and Shaker designs, teaching hundreds of students at his Vermont studio, and placing pieces in the Boston Museum of Fine Arts. George, who grew up in the Woodbury shop, studied industrial design at RISD and worked in product design and architecture before returning to Vermont to establish Sawyer Made as a family-owned workshop.

The workshop produces custom chairs and benches that reinterpret American Windsor and Shaker traditions through traditional green‑woodworking techniques and hand‑cut joinery. Each piece is made to order using sustainably sourced wood, with an emphasis on ethical production and enduring aesthetics. Output is limited to small‑batch, made‑to‑measure seating rather than volume runs; no facility size or headcount figures are published.

The brand has also been featured in design publications such as The New York Times Style Magazine, Domino, Metropolis, and Fine Woodworking, indicating a following among design professionals and collectors.

The founders frame the venture as a re‑envisioning of seating craftsmanship — combining Dave’s technical mastery of Windsor geometry with George’s industrial‑design perspective to create pieces that are “handmade, sustainable, ethically produced, and beautiful.” The business was started to carry forward a living tradition of green woodworking while adapting it for contemporary homes.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom chair making", "Custom bench making", "Windsor chair construction", "Shaker-style seating", "Green woodworking", "Traditional hand joinery", "Sustainable furniture production", "Made-to-order seating"], "industries": ["Residential furniture", "Interior design", "Custom woodworking", "Fine craftsmanship"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Handmade, sustainable, ethically produced construction", "Modern interpretation of American Windsor and Shaker traditions", "Traditional green\u2011woodworking techniques and hand\u2011cut joinery", "Designs rooted in three decades of Windsor chair refinement by Dave Sawyer", "Pieces held in the Boston Museum of Fine Arts collection"], "facts_used": ["East Calais, Vermont headquarters -> db", "Founded 2012 by George Sawyer -> /about", "Dave Sawyer began chairmaking in 1982 -> /about", "Dave Sawyer MIT mechanical engineering degree -> /about", "Dave Sawyer taught chairmaking to hundreds -> /about", "Work in Boston Museum of Fine Arts -> /about", "George Sawyer RISD industrial design -> /about", "George Sawyer launched Sawyer Made in 2012 -> /about", "Custom chairs and benches, Windsor/Shaker tradition -> /", "Handmade, sustainable, ethically produced -> /", "Green woodworking techniques -> /about", "Testimonials from homeowners -> /", "Featured in NY Times Style Magazine, Domino, Metropolis, Fine Woodworking -> /", "Instagram handle sawyer_made -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Sawyer Made custom chairs and benches are a modern take on the American Windsor and Shaker Tradition", "founded_year": "2012", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://instagram.com/sawyer_made"], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sawyer-made' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Schluter''s Metal Artwork and Welding operates from Helena, Montana, where it was founded in 2011 by Colton Schluter, a journeyman-carded welder. After earning a welding degree at VoTech and joining the union in 2012, Schluter worked on refineries and power plants coast to coast, eventually earning his journeyman boilermaker card in 2016. The shop began as a side venture during his union years and became his full-time focus in 2017.

The company provides custom metal fabrication and welding — railings, gates, stairs, structural steel, furniture, and decorative pieces such as wildlife silhouettes, wall art, and custom signs — all cut, bent, and welded in-house from steel, aluminum, and stainless. An on-site powder coating line, operated under the PowderCoating of Helena banner, offers more than 6,500 colors with gloss, matte, texture, and heat-resistant finishes. The shop also coats customer-supplied parts, handling everything from automotive wheels and roll cages to commercial brackets and handrails. To date, the team has completed over 1,000 projects.

Schluter''s serves homeowners, contractors, and commercial builders throughout the Helena area and Lewis & Clark County. Residential clients commission handrails, gates, and artistic metalwork; commercial contractors rely on the shop for structural steel elements, bollards, and brackets. Other fabrication shops without in-house coating send their work to Schluter''s for finishing, and automotive customers bring parts for durable powder coating.

The business emphasizes direct, end-to-end control: every project is custom with no catalog parts, the same shop that fabricates a piece also coats it, and owner Colton Schluter oversees design, fit-up, and finish personally. Quotes are firm, with scope changes discussed before any extra cost.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom metal fabrication", "Welding (steel, aluminum, stainless)", "Powder coating (6,500+ colors, gloss, matte, texture, custom finishes)", "Decorative metalwork (wildlife silhouettes, wall art, custom signs, sculptural pieces)", "Structural steel fabrication (handrails, gates, stairs, bollards, brackets)", "Furniture fabrication", "Automotive parts coating (wheels, brackets, roll cages, frames, suspension components)", "Heat-resistant coatings", "Sandblasting/priming for customer-supplied parts", "Coating for customer-supplied parts", "Commercial structural elements"], "industries": ["Residential construction", "Commercial construction", "Automotive", "Metal fabrication job shops"], "materials": ["Steel", "Aluminum", "Stainless steel"], "equipment": ["In-house powder coating line (PowderCoating of Helena)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Every piece custom, no catalog parts", "In-house powder coating line (PowderCoating of Helena) with 6,500+ colors", "Direct service: owner Colton Schluter oversees every step", "Firm quotes: what we quote is what you pay"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2011 -> /about", "Owner Colton Schluter, journeyman-carded welder -> /about", "Union experience 2012-2017, journeyman boilermaker card 2016 -> /about", "Shop location 4041 Helberg Dr, Helena MT -> /", "Custom fabrication: railings, gates, stairs, structural steel, furniture, decorative art -> /", "Powder coating in-house with 6,500+ colors -> /", "Coats customer-supplied parts -> /", "Serves homeowners, contractors, commercial builders -> /about", "Other fab shops use coating services -> /", "1000+ projects completed -> /", "Direct service, firm quotes, no catalog parts -> /about", "Materials: steel, aluminum, stainless -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Schluter''s Metal Art is a welding and custom fabrication shop in Helena, Montana.", "founded_year": "2011", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='schluter-s-metal-artwork-and-welding' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='SchoolHouse Woodworking operates from Chester Springs, Pennsylvania, where founder Jeff Devlin established the business after a lifelong passion for carpentry that began at age 15. Devlin’s television career on DIY’s Stone House Revival brought wider attention to his focus on historic renovation, but the company remains a deliberately small operation built on personal involvement rather than scale.

The shop specializes in historic restorations, custom cabinetry, furniture making, and kitchen and bath renovations. Work includes period-correct joinery, random-width floorboard installation, fireplace restoration, and the integration of modern appliances within historically accurate cabinetry. Every project is handled directly by Devlin, from initial consultation through on-site execution, with no large crew or subcontracting layers.

Clients are primarily owners of historic homes and properties in southeastern Pennsylvania, including landmark buildings such as the 1735 Drovers Inn, a historic tavern and inn that the company helped restore. The work also extends to hospitality venues seeking period-authentic interiors.

Devlin states that the company was founded on a philosophy of “doing right by the house and the client,” emphasizing complete honesty, a hands-on presence at every stage, and a refusal to take shortcuts. The goal is to leave a legacy of craftsmanship that honors the original structure while meeting modern needs.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Historic restoration", "Custom cabinetry", "Furniture making", "Kitchen renovation", "Bath renovation", "Period-correct joinery", "Random-width floorboard installation", "Fireplace restoration", "Appliance integration within period cabinetry", "Custom woodwork", "Hardware sourcing from local blacksmith"], "industries": ["Historic preservation", "Residential renovation", "Hospitality renovation"], "materials": ["Wood", "Stone", "Brick"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Deliberately small, owner-operated model with no large team", "Owner on-site for every project from consultation to completion", "Commitment to period-accurate details blended with modern convenience", "No shortcuts; complete honesty throughout the process", "Specialization in historic structures such as the 1735 Drovers Inn"], "facts_used": ["Company name and location from database", "Founder Jeff Devlin and company origin story from /about", "30+ years of master craftsmanship claim from homepage and /about", "Services: Historic Restorations, Custom Cabinetry, Furniture, Kitchen and Bath Renovations from homepage", "Address: 368 Exton Square Parkway, Exton, PA 19341 from homepage and /about", "Philosophy: personalized touch, hands-on approach, honesty, no shortcuts from /about", "Small company by design from /about", "Period-correct construction, joinery, random width floorboards, fireplace restoration, appliance integration from homepage", "Historic 1735 Drovers Inn project example from homepage", "Hardware by local blacksmith from homepage"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_pr