UPDATE companies SET description='Seaside Casual Furniture operates from Coventry, Rhode Island, where the brand was officially established in 1996. Its roots trace back to 1911 when Carold "Kit" Arnold opened the Arnold Lumber Company, a sawmill that evolved into a multi-generational family business. In the 1990s, "Art" Arnold Jr. began selling handcrafted mahogany Adirondack chairs from the lumber company''s door shop, turning a hobby into a dedicated furniture line. The company was acquired in 2025 by The Prestwick Companies, a family-owned, Made-in-USA furnishings group based in Sussex, Wisconsin, with manufacturing remaining in Rhode Island.

The company engineers and manufactures luxury outdoor furniture using its proprietary EnviroWood, a non-porous, UV-stabilized recycled HDPE (also called Marine Grade Polymer) developed in 1999 to withstand coastal New England conditions. The product range spans over 400 SKUs, including Adirondack chairs, deep seating, dining and bar sets, fire tables, and planters. All pieces are built at the Rhode Island facility, and the company offers complimentary design services that provide layout planning, finish selection, and 3D renderings before production.

Seaside Casual serves residential homeowners, hospitality operators at high-end resorts and private estates, and commercial projects through a dealer network. Its furniture is specified for environments that demand resistance to salt spray, chlorine, oils, and extreme weather, with substantial weight to stay grounded in high winds.

The brand differentiates itself through a zero-maintenance material that runs UV-inhibited pigment through the entire profile, ensuring color retention for decades. The 1999 material innovation was driven by the need for furniture that could endure corrosive sea air, harsh winters, and relentless sun without sanding, oiling, or covering.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Outdoor furniture manufacturing", "Furniture design and engineering", "Complimentary space planning and design services", "Recycled HDPE (EnviroWood) fabrication", "Custom finish and color selection", "Product care and cleaning product development"], "industries": ["Residential outdoor living", "Hospitality (resorts, private estates)", "Commercial outdoor spaces"], "materials": ["Recycled HDPE (EnviroWood/Marine Grade Polymer)", "Mahogany (historical)", "UV-inhibited pigment"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Zero-maintenance EnviroWood material (UV-stabilized recycled HDPE)", "Color runs solid through entire profile for decades of retention", "Complimentary design services with 3D renderings before production", "Manufacturing in Rhode Island since 1996", "Family-owned heritage dating to 1911"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Coventry, Rhode Island -> db", "Founded 1996 (Seaside Casual officially born) -> /about-us", "Family business rooted in 1911 (Arnold Lumber Company) -> /about-us", "Founder Carold \"Kit\" Arnold opened Arnold Lumber in 1911 -> /about-us", "\"Art\" Arnold Jr. started Adirondack chair hobby in 1990s -> /about-us", "Acquired 2025 by The Prestwick Companies (family-owned, Sussex, WI) -> /about-us", "Manufacturing continues in Rhode Island -> /about-us", "Proprietary EnviroWood/Marine Grade Polymer developed 1999 -> /about-us", "Material: non-porous, UV-stabilized recycled HDPE -> /about-us", "400+ products (SKUs) -> /about-us", "Complimentary design services with 3D renderings -> /", "Serves residential, hos