UPDATE companies SET description='Seneca Foods Corporation, founded in 1949 in Ripon, Wisconsin, is a publicly traded, vertically integrated fruit and vegetable processing company. The business began with a focus on producing seeds, harvesting crops, manufacturing its own containers, and delivering a wide range of nutritious fruit and vegetable products to market.

The company operates a fully integrated model, managing seed production, crop harvesting from over 1,400 family farms, container manufacturing, and processing of fruit and vegetable products. Its portfolio includes well-known brands such as Green Giant, Aunt Nellie''s, Libby''s, CherryMan, Read Salads, Green Valley, and Seneca Snacks. Seneca emphasizes food safety through seven major quality systems and invests in technology for its state-of-the-art facilities across multiple plant locations.

The company''s vertically integrated supply chain allows it to control quality from seed to shelf, providing consistent products such as sweet peas, cherries, and cannellini beans to meet organizational needs.

The company differentiates itself through its "Farm Fresh Goodness Made Great" philosophy, long-standing grower relationships, and commitment to food safety, environmental stewardship, and conservative financial management. Seneca''s fundamental beliefs—honesty, accountability, and respect for growers and employees—have guided its operations since 1949, fostering long-term employee loyalty and shareholder value.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Seed production", "Crop harvesting", "Container manufacturing", "Fruit and vegetable processing", "Canning and packaging", "Food safety and quality systems (seven major quality systems)", "Integrated supply chain management", "Brand management (Green Giant, Aunt Nellie''s, Libby''s, CherryMan, Read Salads, Green Valley, Seneca Snacks)"], "industries": ["Food processing", "Fruit and vegetable processing", "Agriculture (seed production)", "Food manufacturing"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Vertically integrated seed-to-shelf production", "Partnerships with over 1,400 family farms", "In-house container manufacturing", "Seven major food safety quality systems", "Capital investment in state-of-the-art processing facilities"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1949 -> db", "Headquarters Ripon, Wisconsin -> db", "Vertically integrated fruit and vegetable processing company -> /about-us", "Produce seeds, harvest crops, manufacture own containers -> /about-us", "Partnerships with over 1,400 American farms -> /about-us", "Brands: Green Giant, Aunt Nellie''s, Libby''s, CherryMan, Read Salads, Green Valley, Seneca Snacks -> /", "Seven major quality systems for food safety -> /", "Publicly traded company with family pride -> /about-us", "Conservative financial approach, capital investment in technology -> /about-us", "Farm Fresh Goodness Made Great motto -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Seneca Foods is one of the most highly integrated fruit and vegetable processing companies in the US. We manage many\u2014and in some cases all\u2014aspects of production. At Seneca, we produce seeds, harvest crops, manufacture our own containers and provide a wide range of nutritious fruit and vegetable products.", "founded_year": "1949", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='seneca-foods-corporation' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='SenseICs Corporation is based in Columbus, Ohio The company was co-founded by Ramy Tantawy, PhD, and Dale Shane Smith, PhD. Both bring decades of mixed-signal integrated circuit design experience from Intel, Micron, Forza Silicon, and Ohio State University''s Electroscience Lab. The founding year is not publicly disclosed.

As a fabless semiconductor provider, SenseICs designs and develops silicon-verified integrated circuits and microelectronics hardware. Its core technologies include high dynamic range readout integrated circuits (HDR ROICs), tamper-resistant ICs, and wide-band gallium nitride power amplifiers. The company offers full turnkey services from design and tape-out through packaging and test, and supplies evaluation hardware and development kits. Fabrication is typically conducted via multi-project wafer runs with foundry partners such as SkyWater, GlobalFoundries, Tower Semiconductor, and onsemi.

SenseICs serves high-energy physics experiments, medical imaging electronics, and defense and commercial markets. Its customer base includes NASA, the U.S. Navy, Air Force, Army Research Laboratory, CERN, Jefferson Lab, and academic partners at The Ohio State University. The company collaborates closely with OSU''s ElectroScience Laboratory, Nanotech West Lab, and Department of Physics.

The company emphasizes a multidisciplinary approach and a culture summarized by the acronym STRIDE (Staying Curious, Trust, Resilience, Innovation, Diversity, Excellence). It positions its differentiation on radiation-hardening by design for environments exceeding 100 Mrad total ionizing dose, microelectronics, and a team with deep expertise in mixed-signal IC design, RF, and high-speed communication.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Fabless IC design", "Multi-project wafer fabrication coordination", "Design and tape-out for production", "Final product packaging and testing", "Evaluation hardware and development kits", "High dynamic range readout integrated circuits (HDR ROICs)", "Tamper-resistant integrated circuits", "Wide-band gallium nitride power amplifiers", "Radiation-hardening by design (>100 Mrad TID)", "Trusted microelectronics", "High-speed communication IC design", "RF design", "Clock and data recovery (CDR)", "Imaging sensor design", "Diamond particle detectors and electronics", "Medical imaging electronics", "LiDAR IC design", "High radiation environment IC design"], "industries": ["High Energy Physics (HEP) Experiments", "Medical imaging electronics", "Defense", "Commercial", "Government", "Academic research"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Full turnkey integrated circuits and custom microelectronic solutions", "Silicon-verified IC chips with radiation-hardening by design (>100 Mrad TID)", "Trusted microelectronics and tamper-resistant IC technology", "Partnerships with major foundries (SkyWater, GlobalFoundries, Tower, onsemi) and government agencies (NASA, Navy, Air Force, CERN)", "Multidisciplinary team with decades of mixed-signal IC design experience"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Columbus, Ohio -> /about-us", "Co-founders: Ramy Tantawy, PhD and Dale Shane Smith, PhD -> /about-us", "Fabless semiconductor provider of silicon verified IC chips and microelectronics hardware -> /", "Core technologies: HDR ROICs, Tamper Resistant IC, Wide-band GaN Power Amplifiers -> /", "Services: Design & Tape Out, Packaging & Testing, Evaluation hardware -> /", "Industries: High Energy Physics, Medical imaging, Defense, Commercial -> /about-us", "Partners: NASA, Navy, Air Force, ARL, CERN, SkyWater, GlobalFoundries, Tower, onsemi, JeffersonLab, OSU -> /about-us", "Radiation hardening >100 Mrad TID -> /about-us", "Trusted microelectronics -> /about-us", "STRIDE values -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "unclear", "type_evidence": "SenseICs is a fabless semiconductor provider of silicon verified integrated circuit chips and microelectronics hardware.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='senseics-corporation' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Sensible Micro Corporation operates as an independent and authorized electronic component distributor and supply chain solutions partner from its headquarters in Tampa, Florida. The company leverages a global supplier network to deliver local service and quality assurance for a broad range of electronic components.

Its service portfolio includes component sourcing, inventory management and logistics, product lifecycle management, and testing and inspection. The testing lab operates under AS6081, IDEA-QMS-9090B, and ICE-3000 certifications, supporting custom and industry-approved sampling plans. An inventory buy-back program provides an outlet for excess stock. The company distributes active devices such as microcontrollers, memory, and RF components, along with passives and electro-mechanical parts.

Customers span aerospace and defense, automotive and transportation, consumer electronics, energy, industrial, medical, and networking and AI sectors. The client base ranges from large original equipment manufacturers to smaller contract manufacturers seeking a consolidated vendor for electronic components.

