and supply chain solutions partner", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/sensible-micro-corporation/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sensible-micro-corporation' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Sensitron Semiconductor operates from Deer Park, New York, drawing on over 50 years of heritage in high-reliability power electronics. The company''s founding year and original owners are not disclosed in public materials, but it has established itself as a specialist in solid-state power management for demanding markets.

The company designs and manufactures a broad range of power electronic components, including high-power rectifier bridges, lightweight SiC and IGBT power modules, motor controllers, solid-state power controllers, and a full line of JANS QPL diodes and transistors. Its capabilities span custom design, hybrid microelectronics, chip-on-board packaging, power conversion assemblies, and screening and test services such as up-screening commercial discrete parts to military standards. Specific part numbers referenced include the SCP-5282 series TVS modules, SPM1 Series SiC power modules, and SEPD Series solid-state relay power controllers.

Sensitron serves commercial aerospace, space and launch vehicles, defense (aerospace, vehicle, naval, missiles), medical, and high-reliability industrial applications. Its rotating rectifier assemblies are used in aerospace and defense generators rated up to 1000V, 120A, and 27,500 RPM, while its SuperClamp TVS devices protect 115Vac and 270Vdc systems against lightning and voltage spikes per MIL-STD-704, MIL-STD-1399, and DO-160.

The company emphasizes its certifications to MIL-PRF-38534 Class K for hybrid microelectronics and MIL-PRF-19500 for JANS-level discrete diodes, along with AS9100 registration. It highlights patented packaging technology such as the High Strength SMD package, which improves temperature and power cycling performance, and ultralight SiC power bridge modules that deliver high power in a small footprint.', certifications=ARRAY['AS9100','MIL-PRF-38534 Class K','MIL-PRF-19500 (JANTX, JANTXV, JANS)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["High power rectifier bridge design and production", "Motion control and motor controller design", "Solid state power controller (SSPC) design and manufacturing", "Hybrid microelectronics assembly (MIL-PRF-38534 Class K)", "JANS/QPL discrete diode manufacturing (MIL-PRF-19500)", "Screening and test services", "Up-screening/testing of commercial discrete parts", "Custom design and packaging (hybrids, chip-on-board, power conversion)", "EOL replacement / DMS solutions", "High voltage diode assemblies", "Transient voltage suppressor (TVS) module design", "SiC and IGBT power module manufacturing", "Light weight bridge rectifier production", "Power distribution and control modules", "Linear voltage regulators", "Solid state relays and contactor controllers", "Bidirectional current limiters", "Lightning strike protection (LSP) modules", "MIL-STD-704 and MIL-STD-1399 compliant modules", "Performance screening and serialization", "Bare die supply", "Solar array diodes", "SiC Schottky diodes", "SiC MOSFETs", "IGBTs/Thyristors"], "industries": ["Commercial Aerospace", "Space and Launch Vehicles", "Defense Aerospace", "Defense Vehicle", "Defense Naval", "Defense Missiles", "Medical", "High Reliability Industrial", "Industrial Power Generation"], "materials": ["Silicon Carbide (SiC)", "Silicon"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Certified to MIL-PRF-38534 Class K for hybrid microelectronics", "QPL listed to