UPDATE companies SET description='Sequel Wire and Cable LLC was founded in May 2019 when four partners established the company in Argos, Indiana. The venture was led by industry veterans including Rich Carr, who serves as founder and CEO of the OEM group, and Gary Yetman, executive chairman of Sequel Holdings. The leadership team also includes Jim Coleman as president and CEO of the low-voltage group, and Kurt Hennelly as president of Sequel Wire and Cable. Their stated vision was to quickly become a meaningful player in the wire and cable industry by employing the latest technologies, hiring top talent, and maintaining an unrelenting focus on customer care.

The company specializes in the drawing and extrusion of insulated copper wire for OEM and low-voltage markets. Its product lines encompass UL/CSA and SAE compliant wire, as well as low-voltage cables such as CMR, CMP, FPLR, and FPLP types.

Sequel serves a broad set of industries. OEM customers include agricultural equipment, appliance, automotive, battery and electric-vehicle charging, construction equipment, heavy-duty truck, marine, motorcycle, off-road vehicle, RV and trailer, water heater, and welding cable sectors. The low-voltage division supplies security and intrusion, access control, thermostat, fire alarm, audio-visual and sound systems, landscape lighting, and alternative energy markets, including PV cable.

