UPDATE companies SET description='Sider''s Woodcrafting operates from a home-based workshop in Brewer, Maine. The company was founded in October 2015 by Bruce and Mary Graybill after the birth of their first child prompted them to seek ways to save money. Bruce began making cutting boards as Christmas gifts using only a table saw and a belt sander; a friend''s request for eleven more boards sparked the business.

The shop produces handcrafted cutting boards, end-grain chopping blocks, charcuterie boards, specialty shaped boards, epoxy coasters, and desk accessories. All items are made by hand in the small workshop beside the Graybills'' house, using domestic and exotic woods sourced worldwide along with epoxy resin. In its first full year (2016), the company sold nearly 400 cutting boards.

Sider''s Woodcrafting sells directly to consumers through its online store, serving the kitchenware and home-goods markets. Customers include home cooks, gift buyers, and enthusiasts of functional wood art.

