UPDATE companies SET description='Sierra Components Inc. was founded in 1992 in Minden, Nevada, as a family-run business serving the microelectronics industry. What began with a fax machine, a flow hood, and a few nitrogen boxes has grown into a multi-million-dollar distribution and processing facility specializing in silicon wafers and bare die. The company''s president and founder brings over 40 years of bare-die distribution experience and more than 42 years in the microelectronics field.

Today the firm operates as a distribution and processing center, offering visual inspection to MIL-STD-883 Method 2010 and MIL-STD-750 Methods 2072/2073, element evaluation and lot qualification to MIL-PRF-38534D Levels H and K, MIL-PRF-19500, and customer source-control drawings. It also provides alternate-component sourcing, wafer processing such as SAW sort and inspection of wafers to die form and wafer probe, and a surplus-inventory program that stores and sells excess stock with a guaranteed return of at least 50 percent of book value. A partnership with Kooker Technologies adds component design, packaging, and substrate fabrication with fast turnaround times.

Sierra Components serves the microelectronics and semiconductor sectors, including customers who require military-grade qualification to MIL-PRF-38534D and MIL-PRF-19500.

The founder''s stated goal has been to provide top-notch service with a personal touch—no automated attendants, just a real person on the phone. The company describes itself as large enough to handle the task yet small enough to give each customer individual attention, a philosophy reinforced by a staff with over 78 combined years in the semiconductor industry.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Visual inspection (MIL-STD-883 Method 2010)", "Visual inspection (MIL-STD-750 Method 2072/2073)", "Element evaluation (MIL-PRF-38534D Levels H and K)", "Lot qualification (MIL-PRF-38534D)", "Lot qualification (MIL-PRF-19500)", "Source Control Drawing (SCD) qualification", "Alternate component sourcing and research", "Wafer SAW sort and inspection to die form", "Wafer probe", "Surplus inventory management and sales", "Component design and packaging", "Substrate fabrication"], "industries": ["Microelectronics", "Semiconductor"], "materials": ["Silicon wafers", "Bare die"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["No automated attendants; customers always reach a live person", "Large enough to handle the task, small enough for personal attention", "Fast manufacturing turnaround including substrate fabrication via Kooker Technologies partnership", "Surplus inventory program guaranteeing at least 50% of book value return", "Staff with over 78 combined years of semiconductor industry experience"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1992 -> /about", "Family-run business -> /about", "Headquarters in Minden, Nevada -> db", "Distribution and processing facility specializing in silicon wafers and bare die -> /about", "President and founder with 40+ years bare die distribution experience -> /about", "Staff with over 78 combined years in semiconductor industry -> /about", "Visual inspection to MIL-STD-883 Method 2010 -> /services", "Visual inspection to MIL-STD-750 Method 2072/2073 -> /services", "Element evaluation to MIL-PRF-38534D Levels H and K -> /services", "Lot qualification to MIL-PRF-38534D -> /services", "Lot qualification to MIL-PRF-19500 -> /services", "Source Control Drawing qualification -> /services", "Alternate component sourcing and research -> /services", "Wafer SAW sort and inspection to die form -> /services", "Wafer probe -> /services", "Surplus inventory storage and sales with 50% book value return -> /services", "Partnership with Kooker Technologies for component design, packaging, substrate fabrication -> /", "Fast manufacturing turnaround times -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "grown into a multi-million dollar distribution and processing facility specializing in silicon wafers and bare die", "founded_year": "1992", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned", "Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sierra-components-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Sierra Peaks Corporation is headquartered in Albuquerque, New Mexico, with additional facilities in Fairfax, Virginia, and Lemon Grove, California. The company has been designing, engineering, and manufacturing custom system solutions for over four decades, though a specific founding year is not publicly disclosed.

The firm provides full-service engineering and manufacturing, spanning mechanical, electrical, systems, and software design through to machining, welding, electromechanical assembly, modeling, sewing, and custom cable fabrication. Its three sites collectively offer more than 50,000 square feet of manufacturing and program management space, all maintained to NISPOM security standards for restricted programs. Capabilities also include first-article prototyping, inspection simulations, and integration services.

Sierra Peaks serves the defense, intelligence, aerospace, maritime, energy, audio, and research sectors, with highlighted work in national security and aerospace. Customers range from government agencies to commercial organizations requiring highly customized hardware and software solutions, such as aerostructures, automated test equipment, and specialized particulate sampling systems.

The company emphasizes that no two solutions are alike, positioning its differentiation on end-to-end collaboration—from concept and line drawings through prototyping, production, and testing—delivered on time and on budget by dedicated project managers. Its facilities are configured for rapid prototyping, manufacturing, and testing under security clearances.', certifications=ARRAY['NISPOM']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Mechanical engineering", "Electrical engineering", "Systems engineering", "Software engineering", "Machining", "Welding", "Electromechanical assembly", "Modeling", "Sewing", "Custom cable fabrication", "Full-service machine shop", "Inspection simulations", "Engineering integration", "First article prototyping", "Project management", "Rapid prototyping", "Testing", "NISPOM-compliant manufacturing"], "industries": ["Defense", "Intelligence", "Aerospace", "Maritime", "Energy", "Audio", "Research", "National Security"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["50,000+ sq ft manufacturing space across three NISPOM-compliant facilities", "In-house mechanical, electrical, systems, and software engineering", "Full-service machine shop with machining, welding, and electromechanical assembly", "Custom cable fabrication and first-article prototyping", "Project management focused on on-time, on-budget delivery"], "facts_used": ["Headquartered in Albuquerque, NM with facilities in Fairfax, VA and Lemon Grove, CA -> /about", "Over 50,000 sq ft manufacturing space across three states -> /about", "NISPOM compliant facilities for restricted programs -> /about", "Design, engineering, manufacturing of custom system solutions for over 40 years -> /about", "Industries served: defense, intelligence, aerospace, maritime, energy, audio, research -> /", "Processes: machining, welding, electromechanical assembly, modeling, sewing -> /", "Engineering disciplines: mechanical, electrical, systems, software -> /", "P